# Serve the real 404 page, with a 404 status, for anything that does not exist.
#
# Without this the site answered 200 for every URL, including nonsense ones:
#
#   GET /zzz-not-real-9987  ->  200, rendering the home page
#
# That is single-page-application fallback behaviour, and on a static
# multi-page site it lets a crawler index an unbounded number of URLs that
# were never real pages.
#
# Cloudflare Pages matches static assets before a `_redirects` rule, so this
# catch-all only fires when nothing else did. Real pages and their
# directory index files are unaffected.
#
# If deploys still answer 200 for a missing path after this ships, the Pages
# project itself is in SPA mode: turn that off in the dashboard, because that
# setting overrides this file.
/*  /404.html  404
